      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name was officially shortened to Greenup in 1872 to avoid confusion with nearby Greensburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenup%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Greenup sits where the Little Sandy River meets the Ohio River, a natural border that defines the city’s southern edge.",
